   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "thm:regret_rots",
    "number": "Theorem 4",
    "quote": "Let $b_n=(n-1)/n$. ... The regret of Algorithm 1 satisfies the following finite-time bounds: R_{\\mu}(T)=\\sum_{i\\in [K]:\\Delta_i>\\lambda} O(\\Delta_i+\\frac{V\\log(T\\Delta_i^2/V)}{\\Delta_i})+\\max_{i\\in [K],\\Delta_i\\leq \\lambda} \\Delta_i \\cdot T, ... where $\\lambda \\geq 16\\sqrt{V/T}$"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Sub-UCB bound. The O applies to the first sum only. Regret R = T max mu - E[sum r_t], i.e. pseudo-regret."
  },
